{{- /*
The instruction a model is given to fill a caller's schema from a document's text.

  .Citations     whether each value is to name the lines it was read from
  .Instructions  the caller's own instructions; may be empty
  .Schema        the caller's JSON Schema, as text
  .Problems      what an earlier reply got wrong, one per entry; empty on a first attempt
  .Text          the document, one block per line, each line led by its ref in square brackets

The reply shape named below is the one the adapter decodes and the one its
reply schema enforces. Changing it here changes neither.
*/ -}}
Fill the schema below from the document that follows it. Use only what the document says. Where the document does not say, use null.
{{if .Citations}}Every line of the document begins with a ref in square brackets. For each value you fill, list the refs of the lines it was read from.
{{end}}Reply with one JSON object and nothing else: {"data": <the object the schema describes>, "citations": [{"pointer": "<JSON pointer into data>", "refs": ["<ref>"]}]}{{if not .Citations}} with an empty list of citations{{end}}.
